+## Shader resource ownership
+
+`Shader` and `ShaderBundle` implement `IDisposable`; creation, use and release
+must occur on the owning render thread. RenderContext tracks every created
+shader, so a forgotten bundle remains owned until `DisposeShaders()` releases
+all remaining programs and uniform buffers. SDL2/SDL3 normal cleanup calls this
+before native context shutdown, including when the application cleanup hook
+throws. This method closes the shader scope; it does not dispose all other
+render resources. See [the shader lifecycle validation](docs/shader-lifecycle.md).
+Headless lifecycle tests also initialize the native text engine; make the native
+libraries produced by the supported build available on the library search path.
+
+## Runtime tangent geometry
+
+The engine now references the existing `extern/SimpleMesh/SimpleMesh` project
+for managed MikkTSpace. Initialize that submodule before building the client;
+its assembly must be included with the runtime files. `VMeshTangentBuilder`
+creates a separate per-draw FVF3/FVF4 buffer from NORMAL+TEX1/TEX2 data and
+preserves source assets. Authored TEX3/TEX4 data remains untouched. Tangent
+geometry is currently an explicit preparation API. The separate opt-in Surface
+normal-map setting supports FVF3/FVF4 meshes with authored tangents. See
+[the tangent validation](docs/vmesh-tangents.md).
+
+## Explicit Surface GPU uploads
+
+`SurfaceGpuTextureCache` shares supplemental uploads by library file and node,
+and enforces a 256 MiB logical residency budget per resource manager across
+active and fence-retiring entries. `surface_normal_maps` is opt-in and currently
+applies to FVF3/FVF4 meshes with authored tangents; each draw holds a GPU lease
+only for its execution. FVF1/FVF2 tangent generation and a retail NAP visual
+validation remain open.
+[Upload and BC5 sampler validation](docs/surface-gpu-upload.md).
+
+## GPU frame retirement
+
+`RenderContext.RetireAfterFrame` batches release callbacks after the current
+frame's last commands. OpenGL waits for a fence, or uses a synchronous fallback
+without sync support. Normal shutdown drains pending releases before shaders
+and native context shutdown. `SurfaceGpuTexture.RetireAfterFrame` marks its scope
+unavailable immediately and delays physical Dispose; later Dispose cannot bypass
+the fence. [Validation and limits](docs/gpu-frame-retirement.md).
